The pinned upstream archive is unchanged. Fieldkin's derived fixture reorganizes
column files by their original database/table identifiers, interprets InputData
bytes as ISO-8859-1, selects up to 64 evenly spaced line records per column, and
represents blank records as null. It preserves original attribute names and uses
full filenames as stable IDs. Class folders supply evaluation labels only.
Differences between InputData and duplicated Classes values are recorded, and
only InputData values are supplied to matchers. The importer and protocol record
all modifications, source hashes and evaluation limitations.

The upstream README credits Microsoft Northwind and MySQL Sakila demonstration
databases and describes manually grouped schema correspondences and injected
tuples. Its original text remains inside northix.zip. This notice was written
by Fieldkin for attribution and is not presented as an upstream notice. Neither
the creator nor UCI endorses Fieldkin or its evaluation results.
